Author: Aryan Shah <aryan_shah@apple.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 9 11:43:22 2026 +0100

    Validate base64 content (#131)
    
    ### Motivation
    
    We currently ignore unknown characters when parsing the body of a PEM
    document. We should also validate whether the body forms a valid base64
    encoded string.
    
    ### Modifications
    
    - Repurposed the `checkLineLengthsOfBase64EncodedString()` method to
    also return the base64 encoded bytes with the line endings removed.
    - Updated `LazyPEMDocument` to now require base64 encoded bytes
    _without_ line endings.
    - Now that the input doesn't have any line endings, the presence of any
    non-base64 characters must mean that the input has invalid characters.
    - As such, `LazyPEMDocument/decode()` was updated to no longer pass the
    [`.ignoreUnknownCharacters`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/foundation/nsdata/base64decodingoptions/ignoreunknowncharacters)
    option to `Data(base64Encoded:)`.
    - This means that when the body contains non-base64 characters,
    `Data(base64Encoded:)` returns `nil` (we already throw
    `ASN1Error.invalidPEMDocument` when receiving `nil`).
    
    ### Result
    
    Better validation.

